    "https://uzhcareer.ch/de/jobs/detail/?id=5f31919a-d8d6-f111-9b60-9e890cc6b0ac&slug=ai-agent-builder-graduate-opportunity-in-technology-transformation": {
      "title": "AI Agent Builder | Graduate Opportunity in Technology & Transformation",
      "description": "AI Agent Builder | Graduate Opportunity in Technology & Transformation Deloitte 100% Feststelle - Einstiegsstelle Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Beschreibung Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Business Line: Technology & Transformation Location: Zurich & Geneva Work Pattern Percentage: 80-100% Start date: Ongoing Experience Level: Graduate About the Role In Technology & Transformation, you’ll work with colleagues who bring together technology and business perspectives to help clients navigate change. As generative AI moves from experimentation into practical use, we are looking for a curious recent graduate to join our Technology & Transformation team in Switzerland as an AI Agent Engineer. You will help turn promising ideas into AI solutions that improve how we work and support our clients. How you can make an impact Identify high-value opportunities for AI agents and translate business needs into clear use cases. Design and develop AI agents and AI-enabled applications, from rapid prototypes through testing and deployment. Adapting and reusing proven capabilities where appropriate; build reusable assets that improve productivity, quality, knowledge access and client delivery. Test solutions rigorously, iterate based on user feedback and contribute to technical documentation and reusable development patterns. Collaborate with technology, risk and business specialists to progress solutions toward controlled and scalable use and help teams understand what agentic AI can realistically do. What you bring to succeed Recently graduated with a Master’s degree in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Machine Learning, Data Science, Robotics, Computational Science, Software Engineering or another strongly AI/engineering-related field. Hands-on experience developing an AI agent or AI-enabled application for personal, educational, research or professional use. A foundation in software development, together with hands-on exposure to modern generative-AI technologies. The ability to combine engineering discipline with creativity. Having developed an AI agent during your studies, as part of your master’s thesis, during a relevant internship or as a personal project would be an advantage. What sets you apart Experience with some of the following would be valuable: LLM application development and agentic AI Tool/function calling and APIs Retrieval-augmented generation and vector search Prompt and context engineering Git and modern software-development practices AI evaluation and testing Structured and unstructured data processing Cloud or sandbox development environments Your team In the Technology & Transformation business line, we empower organisations to navigate the future through tech-enabled business transformation. That could mean shaping a technology strategy, improving how an organisation works or helping deliver a new solution. You’ll have opportunities to learn from different specialists, contribute your own ideas and build skills through practical project work. Meet our people Want to learn more about what it's really like to work at Deloitte? Hear directly from our Cyber security team: Explore a career in Tech Advisory Technology & Transformation | Deloitte Insights Benefits for you We believe in more than just work – we're committed to creating meaningful, inclusive experiences where you can thrive, both personally and professionally. From flexible working arrangements and continuous learning to comprehensive well-being support and opportunities to make a social impact, we invest in helping you grow. Explore our full benefits package here Careers at Deloitte At Deloitte, your ideas create impact and spark meaningful change for our clients, people and society. Your unique expertise, background, and perspective help us find new ways into the most complex challenges so we can brighten the futures of those our work affects. With more than 460’000 employees globally, Deloitte is the largest professional services firm in the world, with offices in more than 150 countries. In Switzerland, we provide a wide range of integrated services in the areas of Audit & Assurance, Tax & Legal, Strategy, Risk & Transactions, and Technology & Transformation. With around 2,500 employees at six locations, we serve companies and organisations of all sizes in every industry sector. ​Experience endless opportunities for professional growth, where you can bring in your entrepreneurial spirit while advising top-tier organizations on cutting-edge interdisciplinary projects within a global environment. ​ Join a collaborative culture where you can work flexibly alongside talented, inspiring colleagues from over 70 nationalities. We are looking for people who approach challenges with curiosity and flexibility; bring a collaborative mindset and a can-do attitude; and wish to grow their career in a dynamic and fast-paced environment.​ Together makes progress. Want to know more about opportunities at Deloitte? Visit www.deloitte.com/ch/careers . How to apply Ready to make an impact? Apply now! We're looking forward to hearing from you. Please click on “apply now” to submit a complete application, including CV, cover letter, references and degree certificates. What to expect: Learn about our recruitment process and read tips from our recruiters that help you best prepare. Not quite the right fit? Join our Talent Community If you're interested in Deloitte but haven't found the perfect opportunity yet, we'd love to stay in touch. Join our Talent Community to receive personalized job alerts, exclusive insights into our business, and invitations to networking events. Register for our Talent Community If you have any questions, contact Sidorela at talent@deloitte.ch . *We consider all qualified applicants for employment regardless of race, ethnicity, religious beliefs, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age or disability, in accordance with applicable law. Research shows that women are less likely to apply for roles unless they match all the criteria; don’t hold yourself back – apply today. We do not accept applications from recruitment agencies for this position. © 2026. For information, contact Deloitte AG. All rights reserved. Deloitte AG is an equal opportunities employer. Stelle anzeigen Publikationsdatum 03.11.2026 Arbeitspensum (%) 100% Branche Unternehmens- / Strategieberatung Funktionsbereich Beratung, Planung & Strategie Stellenantritt Per sofort Arbeitsort Pfingstweidstrasse 11 8005 Zürich Schweiz Kontaktinformationen Frau Servello Salome 058 279 7796 E-Mail Pfingstweidstrasse 11 8005 Zürich Weitere Jobs Deloitte Career Start: Analyst - Large & Complex Audit - Zurich, Basel & Bern (Start October 2027) (24995) Deloitte 03.11.2026 80% Feststelle - Einstiegsstelle Schweiz Deloitte Intern, Banking Solutions Deloitte 03.11.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Deloitte Intern Transfer Pricing - Tax & Legal 25512 Deloitte 20.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Deloitte Intern - Financial Services Audit - Geneva (January 2027 – June 2027) Deloitte 12.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Westschweiz & Wallis Deloitte Intern – Accounting & Reporting Assurance (February 2027 – July 2027) Deloitte 08.10.2026 80% Praktikum Schweiz Deloitte Intern - LSE/SME - Audit & Assurance (October 2027 – June 2028) Deloitte 07.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen"
