    "https://uzhcareer.ch/de/jobs/detail/?id=e7985784-9cd7-f111-9b60-9e890cc6b0ac&slug=intern-banking-solutions": {
      "title": "Intern, Banking Solutions",
      "description": "Intern, Banking Solutions Deloitte 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Beschreibung Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Location : Zurich Work Pattern Percentage : 80-100% Finding the talent that makes Deloitte unique Are you passionate about the banking industry and driven to help banks transform their business operations? Do you enjoy working in interdisciplinary teams to solve complex challenges, with AI as part of your everyday toolkit? Then join our Banking Solutions team! About the Role As an Intern, you will gain hands-on experience from day one, supporting our clients in end-to-end business transformations, from strategy and target operating model design to process optimisation and technology enablement, with AI embedded throughout. How you can make an impact In your role, you will: Build your knowledge across a broad range of Banking Solutions domains, including Advisory, Front-to-Back Credit & Risk, Banking Technology, and Investment Management Solutions Support our clients in addressing key business challenges and driving sustainable growth by translating strategic priorities into actionable solutions Help banks identify, design and implement AI use cases across the value chain, from AI-enabled processes to intelligent operations Contribute to client engagements through research and analysis, solution design, and the preparation of materials for client meetings, workshops and recommendations Work alongside experienced and motivated practitioners from diverse areas of expertise who are committed to sharing their knowledge and supporting your career development Who we are looking for You hold a university degree in banking, finance, business administration, economics, or a similar field of study You have a genuine passion for the banking industry and an understanding of the trends, challenges, and market dynamics shaping its future You are an analytical and insightful thinker, able to structure complex problems and develop creative solutions You are fluent in both German and English; French or Italian is a plus You are willing to travel within Switzerland and potentially abroad What sets you apart You are an energetic team player with a positive, can-do attitude and strong interpersonal skills, committed to delivering high-quality work You have excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to effectively articulate business problems and recommendations to our clients You actively use AI tools in your daily work, from research and analysis to solution design, and are curious to explore new ways of working You can work independently and recognise when to seek input or support from others Your team Join a diverse, international, and highly motivated team. We will help you grow both personally and professionally through our training, mentoring programmes, and on-the-job learning, while also connecting you with colleagues across all business lines. Benefits for you We believe in more than just work – we're committed to creating meaningful, inclusive experiences where you can thrive, both personally and professionally. From flexible working arrangements and continuous learning to comprehensive well-being support and opportunities to make a social impact, we invest in helping you grow. Explore our full benefits package here Careers at Deloitte At Deloitte, your ideas create impact and spark meaningful change for our clients, people and society. Your unique expertise, background, and perspective help us find new ways into the most complex challenges so we can brighten the futures of those our work affects. With more than 460’000 employees globally, Deloitte is the largest professional services firm in the world, with offices in more than 150 countries. In Switzerland, we provide a wide range of integrated services in the areas of Audit & Assurance, Tax & Legal, Strategy, Risk & Transactions, and Technology & Transformation. With around 2,500 employees at six locations, we serve companies and organisations of all sizes in every industry sector. ​Experience endless opportunities for professional growth, where you can bring in your entrepreneurial spirit while advising top-tier organizations on cutting-edge interdisciplinary projects within a global environment. ​ Join a collaborative culture where you can work flexibly alongside talented, inspiring colleagues from over 70 nationalities. We are looking for people who approach challenges with curiosity and flexibility; bring a collaborative mindset and a can-do attitude; and wish to grow their career in a dynamic and fast-paced environment.​ Together make progress. Want to know more about opportunities at Deloitte? Visit www.deloitte.com/ch/careers. How to apply Ready to make an impact? Apply now! We're looking forward to hearing from you. Please click on “apply now” to submit a complete application, including CV, cover letter, references and degree certificates. What to expect: Learn about our recruitment process and read tips from our recruiters that help you best prepare. Not quite the right fit? Join our Talent Community If you're interested in Deloitte but haven't found the perfect opportunity yet, we'd love to stay in touch. Join our Talent Community to receive personalized job alerts, exclusive insights into our business, and invitations to networking events. Register for our Talent Community If you have any questions, contact Sidorela at talent@deloitte.ch . *We consider all qualified applicants for employment regardless of race, ethnicity, religious beliefs, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age or disability, in accordance with applicable law. Research shows that women are less likely to apply for roles unless they match all the criteria; don’t hold yourself back – apply today. We do not accept applications from recruitment agencies for this position. © 2026. For information, contact Deloitte AG. All rights reserved. Deloitte AG is an equal opportunities employer. Stelle anzeigen Publikationsdatum 03.11.2026 Arbeitspensum (%) 100% Branche Unternehmens- / Strategieberatung Funktionsbereich Rechnungswesen & Controlling Stellenantritt Nach Vereinbarung Arbeitsort Pfingstweidstrasse 11 8005 Zürich Schweiz Kontaktinformationen Frau Sidorela Ustali E-Mail Pfingstweidstrasse 11 8005 Zürich Weitere Jobs Deloitte Career Start: Analyst - Large & Complex Audit - Zurich, Basel & Bern (Start October 2027) (24995) Deloitte 03.11.2026 80% Feststelle - Einstiegsstelle Schweiz Deloitte AI Agent Builder | Graduate Opportunity in Technology & Transformation Deloitte 03.11.2026 100% Feststelle - Einstiegsstelle Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Deloitte Intern Transfer Pricing - Tax & Legal 25512 Deloitte 20.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen Deloitte Intern - Financial Services Audit - Geneva (January 2027 – June 2027) Deloitte 12.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Westschweiz & Wallis Deloitte Intern – Accounting & Reporting Assurance (February 2027 – July 2027) Deloitte 08.10.2026 80% Praktikum Schweiz Deloitte Intern - LSE/SME - Audit & Assurance (October 2027 – June 2028) Deloitte 07.10.2026 100% Praktikum Schweiz - Zürich & Schaffhausen"
